  "editorial_identity": "Cartographic documentary brand across two documentary formats (9:16 portrait and 16:9 landscape): story-first directing in which each narration's own question, withheld answer, and ending note determine the structure, hook mechanism, signature image, surface count, colour casting, and ending (see DIRECTING.md), rendered with a graded marine deep-teal satellite relief spine (#083847 over #03161F ground) that usually carries 70-90% of runtime as a continuous virtual-camera take, plus story-motivated switches to dark vector, parchment, cross-section, horizon terrain, aerial ortho, globe, or real-footage registers; documentary, wry, or comic registers chosen from the narration's tone (flat vector characters, flag avatars, reaction faces, and speech-bubble gags when the story carries irony); per-entity colour casting with rimmed territory fills and three-layer luminous borders and routes; one graphic event per stressed noun with visuals leading the spoken word by 0-0.9 s; axis-aligned in-world map typography; plain true-centered 2-4 word captions at y 70-72% with short opacity fade-in and hard-cut or brief fade-out transitions; zero default watermark; no call-to-action outro; narration-led pacing with visual-locked kinetic SFX.",
